# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your real values.
#
# This connector runs one Gmail MCP server instance PER account so Claude can
# scan several Gmail inboxes at once. Each account authenticates with its own
# stored credentials file, but they all share a single Google Cloud OAuth app.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GMAIL_OAUTH_PATH — path to your Google Cloud OAuth *app* keys file
# (usually named "gcp-oauth.keys.json"). This is shared by every account.
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com and create (or pick) a project.
#   2. Enable the "Gmail API" for that project.
#   3. Under "APIs & Services -> Credentials", create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID
#      of type "Desktop app" and download the JSON.
#   4. Save it somewhere safe and point GMAIL_OAUTH_PATH at it.
GMAIL_OAUTH_PATH=/absolute/path/to/gcp-oauth.keys.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GMAIL_*_CREDENTIALS_PATH — where each account's login token is stored.
# These files are CREATED for you the first time you authenticate an account
# (see the README). Give each account a distinct path so they don't overwrite
# each other. Treat them like passwords and NEVER commit the real files.
GMAIL_PERSONAL_CREDENTIALS_PATH=/absolute/path/to/credentials-personal.json
GMAIL_WORK_CREDENTIALS_PATH=/absolute/path/to/credentials-work.json
